\description{
Read the PTM site occupancy of a MetaMorpheus AllQuantifiedProteinGroups.tsv as one row per group, sample group, basis and modified site.

MetaMorpheus writes each protein group's modification-site occupancy into two cells per sample
group - by PSM count and by intensity - in a compact text form. This reads them as one row per
group, sample group, basis and modified site.
}
\details{
\strong{Read each basis for what it is exact in.} On \code{basis == "count"} rows \code{numerator} and
\code{denominator} are exact PSM counts and \code{fraction} is rounded; on \code{basis == "intensity"} rows
\code{fraction} is exact and the two intensities are rounded.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_occupancy_records}. \code{record_count} counts the protein groups in the whole
  file; \code{returned_count} the groups read, starting \code{offset} groups in; \code{row_count} the rows in
  \code{records}. \code{truncated_cell_count} counts occupancy cells MetaMorpheus cut short, in cells.

  \code{records} has one row per group, sample group, basis and site: \code{fraction} from 0 to 1, and
  \code{numerator} and \code{denominator} in PSMs on count rows or in intensity on intensity rows.
  \code{position} is the 1-based residue; \code{cell_is_truncated} marks a row from a cut cell.
  \code{rows_not_read} is \code{NA}: rows are not counted for this table.

}
\section{entity_index is not an accession index}{


An entity with no modified sites is dropped from the cell, so \code{entity_index} cannot be zipped
with the accessions in \code{protein_group_name}.

}
